+ ```tabular

- column  Code
- column  Reason
- column  Meaning
- column  Message
- column  Resolution
- row  `↯/s.123.1.1`  `CannotExecuteGit`  The `git` command itself could not be executed: no `git` binary was found on the search path, or it could not be started.  `` [↯/s.123.1.1] the Git operation could not be completed because the `git` command could not be executed ``  Install Git, or supply `Commandline.Command` with the path of the binary.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.2`  `NoRepository`  The path opened as a repository is not one: neither a bare repository, a `.git/` directory, a working tree containing one, nor a linked worktree's `<worktree>/.git` file.  `[↯/s.123.1.2] the Git operation could not be completed because /tmp/x is not a Git repository`  Open a path that `git rev-parse --git-dir` would accept, or initialize one with `Git.init`.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.3`  `NoWorktree`  A bare repository was opened as a `Git.Worktree`, which needs an index and working files.  `[↯/s.123.1.3] the Git operation could not be completed because the repository has no working tree`  Open it as a `Git.Repo` instead, or open a linked worktree of it.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.4`  `Moved`  A compare-and-swap failed: the ref held a different value from the `Stale` one the operation was conditional on. Another process moved it between the read and the write.  `[↯/s.123.1.4] the Git operation could not be completed because refs/heads/main was 3f2a… when read but is now 9c1d…`  Read the ref again, decide whether the operation still applies, and retry with the fresh value.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.5`  `NoSuchRef`  A revision or reference named in the operation does not exist.  `[↯/s.123.1.5] the Git operation could not be completed because the reference refs/heads/feature does not exist`  Check the name; `resolve` returns `Unset` rather than raising for a probe.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.6`  `NoSuchObject`  No object with the given hash is in the object database, or it is not of the kind requested.  `[↯/s.123.1.6] the Git operation could not be completed because the object 5c1d… does not exist`  Fetch the object, or check the hash.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.7`  `RefExists`  A ref was to be created, but one of that name already exists.  `[↯/s.123.1.7] the Git operation could not be completed because the reference refs/tags/v1 already exists`  Choose another name, or delete the existing ref first.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.8`  `Unmerged`  A branch was to be deleted without `force`, but its tip is not reachable from HEAD, so the deletion would lose commits.  `[↯/s.123.1.8] the Git operation could not be completed because the branch feature at 3f2a… is not fully merged`  Merge the branch first, or delete it with `force = true`.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.9`  `Conflict`  An operation which cannot stop for conflicts (a fast-forward-only pull, a stash pop that must apply cleanly) met conflicting changes.  `[↯/s.123.1.9] the Git operation could not be completed because there are conflicts in a, b`  Resolve the conflicts through an operation that can stop, such as `merge`, which reports them as a `Stopped` outcome.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.10`  `NothingToCommit`  A commit was requested whose tree is identical to its parent's, and empty commits were not allowed.  `[↯/s.123.1.10] the Git operation could not be completed because there is nothing to commit`  Stage a change, or pass `allowEmpty = true`.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.11`  `Detached`  The operation needs HEAD to be on a branch, and it is detached.  `[↯/s.123.1.11] the Git operation could not be completed because HEAD is detached`  Switch to a branch first.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.12`  `Dirty`  Local changes to the listed files would be overwritten by the operation.  `[↯/s.123.1.12] the Git operation could not be completed because local changes would be overwritten in a, b`  Commit, stash or restore the files first.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.13`  `NotFastForward`  A fast-forward was required (by `FastForward.Only`, or by a remote refusing a non-fast-forward push) and the histories have diverged.  `[↯/s.123.1.13] the Git operation could not be completed because the update is not a fast-forward`  Merge or rebase first, or force the update if that is what is meant.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.14`  `OutsideWorktree`  A path given to a working-tree operation lies outside the working tree.  `[↯/s.123.1.14] the Git operation could not be completed because /etc/passwd is outside the working tree`  Use a path formed from the worktree handle.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.15`  `Untracked`  A path given to an operation on tracked files is not tracked.  `[↯/s.123.1.15] the Git operation could not be completed because loose is not tracked`  Add the file first, or use an operation for untracked files such as `clean`.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.16`  `NoOperationInProgress`  `continue`, `skip`, `abandon` or `quit` was called with no merge, rebase, cherry-pick or revert in progress.  `[↯/s.123.1.16] the Git operation could not be completed because no merge, rebase, cherry-pick or revert is in progress`  Check `operation()` before continuing.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.17`  `OperationInProgress`  A new operation was started while a merge, rebase, cherry-pick or revert was still stopped.  `[↯/s.123.1.17] the Git operation could not be completed because an operation is already in progress`  Continue or abandon the operation in progress first.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.18`  `NoSuchRemote`  The named remote is not configured.  `[↯/s.123.1.18] the Git operation could not be completed because the remote origin does not exist`  Add it with `addRemote`.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.19`  `RemoteExists`  A remote was to be added under a name already in use.  `[↯/s.123.1.19] the Git operation could not be completed because the remote origin already exists`  Choose another name, or use `setRemoteUrl`.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.20`  `Unauthorized`  The remote refused the credentials offered, or asked for some and none were available.  `[↯/s.123.1.20] the Git operation could not be completed because authentication with origin failed`  Configure credentials for the remote.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.21`  `Unreachable`  The remote could not be reached: its host did not resolve, or refused or timed out the connection.  `[↯/s.123.1.21] the Git operation could not be completed because the remote origin could not be reached`  Check the URL and the network.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.22`  `RemoteRejected`  The remote accepted the connection but refused to update the ref, for the reason it gave.  `[↯/s.123.1.22] the Git operation could not be completed because the remote rejected refs/heads/main: pre-receive hook declined`  Read the reason; it is the remote's policy.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.23`  `LeaseFailed`  A push with `Push.Force.Lease` found the remote's ref at a different value from the one expected.  `[↯/s.123.1.23] the Git operation could not be completed because the remote's refs/heads/main was expected to be 3f2a… but is 9c1d…`  Fetch, reconsider, and push with a fresh expectation.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.24`  `NoteNotFound`  `content` was called on a note reference, and no note is attached to the commit in that namespace.  `[↯/s.123.1.24] the Git operation could not be completed because no note was attached to the given object`  Use `note`, which returns `Unset` rather than raising.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.25`  `NoSuchConfig`  A configuration key the operation needs is not set anywhere git would look; typically `user.name` or `user.email` for a commit.  `[↯/s.123.1.25] the Git operation could not be completed because the configuration key user.email is not set`  Set it with `configure`, or in the global configuration.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.26`  `InvalidConfig`  A configuration key or value is malformed: a key with no section, say.  `[↯/s.123.1.26] the Git operation could not be completed because nosection is not a valid value for `  Use a `section.name` or `section.subsection.name` key.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.27`  `BadSignature`  A signature on a commit or tag did not verify.  `[↯/s.123.1.27] the Git operation could not be completed because the signature could not be verified: …`  Check the signer's key is trusted, and that the object has not been altered.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.28`  `SigningFailed`  The signer could not produce a signature.  `[↯/s.123.1.28] the Git operation could not be completed because the object could not be signed: …`  Check the signing key and the signing program.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.29`  `Unsupported`  The backend in use does not implement the operation.  `[↯/s.123.1.29] the Git operation could not be completed because skipping is not supported by this backend`  Use the other backend, or a different operation.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.30`  `Unexpected`  git failed in a way the reason table does not recognise; the error's `detail` carries git's own message.  `[↯/s.123.1.30] the Git operation could not be completed because git reported an unexpected failure`  Read the `detail`.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.31`  `NoteExists`  A note was to be added to a commit which already has one in that namespace, without `force`.  `[↯/s.123.1.31] the Git operation could not be completed because a note is already attached to 5c1d…`  Pass `force = true` to replace it, or use `appendNote`.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.32`  `NoSuchWorktree`  The path given is not a linked working tree of the repository.  `[↯/s.123.1.32] the Git operation could not be completed because /tmp/x is not a linked working tree`  List the worktrees with `worktrees()`.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.33`  `NoSuchStash`  The stash entry no longer exists: it was popped or dropped since it was listed.  `[↯/s.123.1.33] the Git operation could not be completed because the stash entry does not exist`  List the stashes again.
- row  `↯/s.123.1.34`  `Locked`  A lock file (`<ref>.lock`, `index.lock` or `config.lock`) exists: another process is writing the same ref, index or configuration file, or crashed and left the lock behind.  `[↯/s.123.1.34] the Git operation could not be completed because the lock file for refs/heads/main is held by another process`  Retry once the other process has finished; if no process holds it, remove the stale lock file by hand.
+ column  Codice
+ column  Motivo
+ column  Significato
+ column  Messaggio
+ column  Soluzione
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.1`  `CannotExecuteGit`  Non è stato possibile eseguire il comando `git` stesso: nessun binario `git` è stato trovato nel percorso di ricerca, oppure non è stato possibile avviarlo.  `` [↯/s.123.1.1] the Git operation could not be completed because the `git` command could not be executed ``  Installare Git, oppure fornire `Commandline.Command` con il percorso del binario.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.2`  `NoRepository`  Il percorso aperto come repository non lo è: né un repository bare, né una directory `.git/`, né un albero di lavoro che ne contiene una, né il file `<worktree>/.git` di un worktree collegato.  `[↯/s.123.1.2] the Git operation could not be completed because /tmp/x is not a Git repository`  Aprire un percorso che `git rev-parse --git-dir` accetterebbe, oppure inizializzarne uno con `Git.init`.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.3`  `NoWorktree`  Un repository bare è stato aperto come `Git.Worktree`, che richiede un indice e dei file di lavoro.  `[↯/s.123.1.3] the Git operation could not be completed because the repository has no working tree`  Aprirlo invece come `Git.Repo`, oppure aprirne un worktree collegato.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.4`  `Moved`  Un compare-and-swap è fallito: il ref conteneva un valore diverso da quello `Stale` a cui l'operazione era condizionata. Un altro processo lo ha spostato tra la lettura e la scrittura.  `[↯/s.123.1.4] the Git operation could not be completed because refs/heads/main was 3f2a… when read but is now 9c1d…`  Rileggere il ref, decidere se l'operazione si applica ancora, e riprovare con il valore aggiornato.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.5`  `NoSuchRef`  Una revisione o un riferimento nominato nell'operazione non esiste.  `[↯/s.123.1.5] the Git operation could not be completed because the reference refs/heads/feature does not exist`  Controllare il nome; per un sondaggio, `resolve` restituisce `Unset` anziché sollevare.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.6`  `NoSuchObject`  Nel database degli oggetti non c'è alcun oggetto con l'hash dato, oppure non è del genere richiesto.  `[↯/s.123.1.6] the Git operation could not be completed because the object 5c1d… does not exist`  Recuperare l'oggetto con un fetch, oppure controllare l'hash.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.7`  `RefExists`  Si doveva creare un ref, ma ne esiste già uno con quel nome.  `[↯/s.123.1.7] the Git operation could not be completed because the reference refs/tags/v1 already exists`  Scegliere un altro nome, oppure eliminare prima il ref esistente.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.8`  `Unmerged`  Si doveva eliminare un branch senza `force`, ma la sua punta non è raggiungibile da HEAD, quindi l'eliminazione perderebbe dei commit.  `[↯/s.123.1.8] the Git operation could not be completed because the branch feature at 3f2a… is not fully merged`  Fare prima il merge del branch, oppure eliminarlo con `force = true`.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.9`  `Conflict`  Un'operazione che non può fermarsi per i conflitti (un pull solo fast-forward, uno stash pop che deve applicarsi senza problemi) ha incontrato modifiche in conflitto.  `[↯/s.123.1.9] the Git operation could not be completed because there are conflicts in a, b`  Risolvere i conflitti tramite un'operazione che può fermarsi, come `merge`, che li segnala come esito `Stopped`.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.10`  `NothingToCommit`  È stato richiesto un commit il cui albero è identico a quello del genitore, e i commit vuoti non erano consentiti.  `[↯/s.123.1.10] the Git operation could not be completed because there is nothing to commit`  Mettere in stage una modifica, oppure passare `allowEmpty = true`.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.11`  `Detached`  L'operazione richiede che HEAD sia su un branch, ed è invece staccato.  `[↯/s.123.1.11] the Git operation could not be completed because HEAD is detached`  Passare prima a un branch.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.12`  `Dirty`  Le modifiche locali ai file elencati verrebbero sovrascritte dall'operazione.  `[↯/s.123.1.12] the Git operation could not be completed because local changes would be overwritten in a, b`  Fare prima il commit, lo stash o il ripristino dei file.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.13`  `NotFastForward`  Era richiesto un fast-forward (da `FastForward.Only`, o da un remote che rifiuta un push non fast-forward) e le cronologie sono divergenti.  `[↯/s.123.1.13] the Git operation could not be completed because the update is not a fast-forward`  Fare prima un merge o un rebase, oppure forzare l'aggiornamento se è questo che si intende.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.14`  `OutsideWorktree`  Un percorso dato a un'operazione sull'albero di lavoro si trova al di fuori dell'albero di lavoro.  `[↯/s.123.1.14] the Git operation could not be completed because /etc/passwd is outside the working tree`  Usare un percorso formato a partire dall'handle del worktree.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.15`  `Untracked`  Un percorso dato a un'operazione sui file tracciati non è tracciato.  `[↯/s.123.1.15] the Git operation could not be completed because loose is not tracked`  Aggiungere prima il file, oppure usare un'operazione per i file non tracciati come `clean`.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.16`  `NoOperationInProgress`  `continue`, `skip`, `abandon` o `quit` è stato chiamato senza alcun merge, rebase, cherry-pick o revert in corso.  `[↯/s.123.1.16] the Git operation could not be completed because no merge, rebase, cherry-pick or revert is in progress`  Controllare `operation()` prima di continuare.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.17`  `OperationInProgress`  È stata avviata una nuova operazione mentre un merge, un rebase, un cherry-pick o un revert era ancora fermo.  `[↯/s.123.1.17] the Git operation could not be completed because an operation is already in progress`  Continuare o abbandonare prima l'operazione in corso.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.18`  `NoSuchRemote`  Il remote nominato non è configurato.  `[↯/s.123.1.18] the Git operation could not be completed because the remote origin does not exist`  Aggiungerlo con `addRemote`.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.19`  `RemoteExists`  Si doveva aggiungere un remote con un nome già in uso.  `[↯/s.123.1.19] the Git operation could not be completed because the remote origin already exists`  Scegliere un altro nome, oppure usare `setRemoteUrl`.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.20`  `Unauthorized`  Il remote ha rifiutato le credenziali offerte, oppure ne ha chieste e non ce n'erano di disponibili.  `[↯/s.123.1.20] the Git operation could not be completed because authentication with origin failed`  Configurare le credenziali per il remote.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.21`  `Unreachable`  Non è stato possibile raggiungere il remote: il suo host non si è risolto, oppure ha rifiutato la connessione o è andato in timeout.  `[↯/s.123.1.21] the Git operation could not be completed because the remote origin could not be reached`  Controllare l'URL e la rete.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.22`  `RemoteRejected`  Il remote ha accettato la connessione ma si è rifiutato di aggiornare il ref, per il motivo che ha indicato.  `[↯/s.123.1.22] the Git operation could not be completed because the remote rejected refs/heads/main: pre-receive hook declined`  Leggere il motivo; è la politica del remote.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.23`  `LeaseFailed`  Un push con `Push.Force.Lease` ha trovato il ref del remote a un valore diverso da quello atteso.  `[↯/s.123.1.23] the Git operation could not be completed because the remote's refs/heads/main was expected to be 3f2a… but is 9c1d…`  Fare un fetch, riconsiderare, e fare il push con un'attesa aggiornata.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.24`  `NoteNotFound`  `content` è stato chiamato su un riferimento a una nota, e nessuna nota è associata al commit in quel namespace.  `[↯/s.123.1.24] the Git operation could not be completed because no note was attached to the given object`  Usare `note`, che restituisce `Unset` anziché sollevare.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.25`  `NoSuchConfig`  Una chiave di configurazione necessaria all'operazione non è impostata in nessuno dei luoghi in cui git cercherebbe; di solito `user.name` o `user.email` per un commit.  `[↯/s.123.1.25] the Git operation could not be completed because the configuration key user.email is not set`  Impostarla con `configure`, oppure nella configurazione globale.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.26`  `InvalidConfig`  Una chiave o un valore di configurazione è malformato: per esempio, una chiave senza sezione.  `[↯/s.123.1.26] the Git operation could not be completed because nosection is not a valid value for `  Usare una chiave `section.name` o `section.subsection.name`.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.27`  `BadSignature`  La firma su un commit o su un tag non è stata verificata.  `[↯/s.123.1.27] the Git operation could not be completed because the signature could not be verified: …`  Controllare che la chiave del firmatario sia fidata, e che l'oggetto non sia stato alterato.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.28`  `SigningFailed`  Il firmatario non è riuscito a produrre una firma.  `[↯/s.123.1.28] the Git operation could not be completed because the object could not be signed: …`  Controllare la chiave di firma e il programma di firma.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.29`  `Unsupported`  Il backend in uso non implementa l'operazione.  `[↯/s.123.1.29] the Git operation could not be completed because skipping is not supported by this backend`  Usare l'altro backend, oppure un'operazione diversa.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.30`  `Unexpected`  git è fallito in un modo che la tabella dei motivi non riconosce; il `detail` dell'errore porta il messaggio di git stesso.  `[↯/s.123.1.30] the Git operation could not be completed because git reported an unexpected failure`  Leggere il `detail`.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.31`  `NoteExists`  Si doveva aggiungere una nota a un commit che ne ha già una in quel namespace, senza `force`.  `[↯/s.123.1.31] the Git operation could not be completed because a note is already attached to 5c1d…`  Passare `force = true` per sostituirla, oppure usare `appendNote`.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.32`  `NoSuchWorktree`  Il percorso dato non è un albero di lavoro collegato del repository.  `[↯/s.123.1.32] the Git operation could not be completed because /tmp/x is not a linked working tree`  Elencare i worktree con `worktrees()`.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.33`  `NoSuchStash`  La voce dello stash non esiste più: è stata estratta o eliminata da quando è stata elencata.  `[↯/s.123.1.33] the Git operation could not be completed because the stash entry does not exist`  Elencare di nuovo gli stash.
+ row  `↯/s.123.1.34`  `Locked`  Esiste un file di lock (`<ref>.lock`, `index.lock` o `config.lock`): un altro processo sta scrivendo lo stesso ref, indice o file di configurazione, oppure si è bloccato lasciandosi dietro il lock.  `[↯/s.123.1.34] the Git operation could not be completed because the lock file for refs/heads/main is held by another process`  Riprovare quando l'altro processo ha terminato; se nessun processo lo detiene, rimuovere a mano il file di lock stantio.

